course: dictionary
lesson: 3472
title: Fake: not real, and how to spot it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fake means not real. Something fake is made to look like something else, often to trick people. «The famous 1934 Loch Ness monster photo was a fake made with a toy.» The photo looked like a real monster, but it was a toy, so it was not real.
explain: Fake can also be a noun or a verb. A fake is a copy made to trick people, like a fake painting. To fake something means to make a copy to trick people, or to pretend to have a feeling or an illness. «Anxiety and panic attacks are a real illness, not faking» tells you that faking here means pretending to be ill.
explain: Use the context clues to check. Look for words like copy, trick, pretend or real. Then swap in your meaning: does «not real» still make sense in the sentence? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Fake is not always bad. Fake fur and fake plants are harmless. But fake news, fake websites and fake messages can trick you, so check with a trusted source and ask an adult before you believe or share them.
fact: Fake means not real, made to look like something else.
fact: A fake is a copy made to trick people, such as a fake painting or fake money.
fact: «Fake news» means stories that are not true, often written to grab your attention.
fact: «Other reef animals win by tricks: a fake eye near the tail». Here the eye is not a real eye, but it is made to look like one to fool other animals.
fact: Fake messages may try to steal your passwords, so never share a password, and check with an adult if you are not sure.
exercise: «The famous 1934 Loch Ness monster photo was a fake made with a toy.» What does fake mean here? | A kind of fish that lives in lakes | *Not real, made to look like something else | Very old and valuable
exercise: «Codes and currency sold cheaply by other kids or strangers are often stolen or fake; only official shops are safe.» What is the safest choice? | Buy codes from strangers because they are cheap | Trust every message you get | *Buy only from official shops | Share your password to save time
exercise: Ella says, «That smile was fake.» What does she mean? | The smile was very big and bright | The smile was real and happy | *The smile was not real, and the person was pretending to be happy | The smile came from a clown
test: «Anxiety and panic attacks are a real illness, not faking.» What does faking mean here? | Being really ill | *Pretending to be ill | Getting better quickly | Going to the doctor
test: Which phrase means stories that are not true? | Fake fur | Trusted news | Real news | *Fake news
exam: In «a shocking post that is on no trusted news site is probably fake», what should you do? | Copy it into your homework | Believe every word because it is shocking | Share it with everyone quickly | *Check with a trusted source and ask an adult
